@page
@model CampusFlow.Web.Pages.Admin.Housing.AssignmentsModel
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Housing Assignments"; }
@section styles { <link rel="stylesheet" href="~/Pages/Admin/Housing/Assignments.css" asp-append-version="true" /> }
@section scripts { <script src="~/Pages/Admin/Housing/Assignments.js" asp-append-version="true"></script> }
<div id="housing-workspace" data-environment="@Model.EnvironmentName">
    @Html.AntiForgeryToken()
    <header><p class="housing-eyebrow">HOUSING</p><h1>Housing assignments</h1>
        <p>Plan room assignments together. Save changes here before reviewing what needs to change in Elements.</p></header>
    @if (Model.CanApplyToElements)
    {
        <div class="alert alert-warning">Applying a draft changes room assignments in Elements and replaces the affected students' unposted housing batch charges with separate CampusFlow-calculated charges. Posted transactions and other students' charges are not changed. Reviewed capacity changes are saved to this housing period in Elements. Notes stay in CampusFlow. A partial apply preserves the saved plan and requires review before recovery.</div>
    }
    else
    {
        <div class="alert alert-info">Draft workspace: saving does not change Elements. Live sync is not enabled here.</div>
    }
    <div id="housing-message" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
    <div class="housing-toolbar">
        <label>Housing period <select id="housing-period" class="form-select"><option value="">Choose a period</option></select></label>
        <button id="housing-refresh" class="btn btn-outline-primary" type="button" disabled>Refresh from Elements</button>
        <button id="housing-save" class="btn btn-primary" type="button" disabled>Save draft</button>
        <button id="housing-preview" class="btn btn-outline-primary" type="button" disabled>Review changes</button>
        @if (Model.CanApplyToElements)
        {
            <button id="housing-apply" class="btn btn-danger" type="button" disabled>Apply assignments and charges to Elements</button>
        }
    </div>
    <p id="housing-summary"></p>
    @if (Model.CanApplyToElements)
    {
        <section id="housing-recovery" class="alert alert-warning" hidden aria-labelledby="housing-recovery-title">
            <h2 id="housing-recovery-title">Review a partial apply</h2>
            <p id="housing-recovery-failure"></p>
            <p>The saved assignments are retained. Recovery supports added commuter assignments only. Moves, removals, capacity changes, residential charges or conflicting live assignments need administrator review.</p>
            <p>If a period was reinitialized, recovery can explicitly deallocate its reviewed deleted commuter records before applying the remaining assignments. Active room assignments are preserved. The preview shows how many historical records require this step.</p>
            <button id="housing-review-recovery" type="button" class="btn btn-outline-primary">Review recovery</button>
            <div id="housing-recovery-preview" hidden>
                <p id="housing-recovery-counts"></p>
                <p>Already completed assignments will be checked and skipped. The remaining assignments will be submitted. CampusFlow will check and reconcile the affected students’ unposted managed housing batch entries to no housing charge; manual and posted entries remain protected.</p>
                <label>Review reason <textarea id="housing-recovery-reason" class="form-control" maxlength="500" rows="2"></textarea></label>
                <label class="d-block"><input id="housing-recovery-confirmed" type="checkbox" /> I reviewed the live assignments and housing batch and want to resume this saved plan.</label>
                <button id="housing-resume" type="button" class="btn btn-danger" disabled>Resume remaining commuter assignments</button>
            </div>
        </section>
    }
    <section id="housing-setup" class="alert alert-info" aria-live="polite" hidden>
        <strong>Commuter room setup for this period</strong>
        <p id="housing-setup-counts"></p>
        <div id="housing-setup-missing" hidden>
            <p>These rooms exist under Properties in Elements but are not included in this housing period:</p>
            <ul id="housing-setup-rooms"></ul>
            <p>Update the housing period’s property setup in Elements, then refresh CampusFlow. Refresh reads the period’s rooms; it does not add master rooms. Review existing assignments before reinitializing a housing period.</p>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section id="housing-capacity-warning" class="housing-capacity-warning" role="alert" hidden>
        <strong id="housing-capacity-title"></strong>
        <p>These assignments came from Elements. You can review and save the draft, but New assignments cannot exceed capacity. An unrelated existing violation does not block fixing another room. Capacity edits must accommodate the occupants remaining in that room.</p>
        <ul id="housing-capacity-list"></ul>
    </section>
    <p>Elements supports 1–10 students per room. For larger commuter groups, set up multiple rooms under Commuter or Commuter Dorm in Elements and include them in the selected housing period, then refresh this period. Commuter rooms create no CampusFlow housing charge and do not use intentional-single rates.</p>
    <p>CampusFlow uses the amounts saved in <a href="~/Admin/Housing/Fees">Housing Fee Setup</a>, not the Elements room rate. Save a fee schedule for this term before applying assignments. Intentional-single charges appear as separate lines. Refreshed assignments start with the Standard rate choice.</p>
    <div class="housing-toolbar">
        <label>Dorm <select id="housing-dorm" class="form-select"><option value="">All Dorms</option></select></label>
        <label>Filter assignments <input id="housing-filter" class="form-control" type="search" placeholder="Building, room, student, rate, or notes" /></label>
        <button id="housing-clear" class="btn btn-outline-danger" type="button" disabled>Clear selected assignments</button>
    </div>
    <section id="housing-bulk" class="housing-bulk" aria-labelledby="housing-bulk-title">
        <div><h2 id="housing-bulk-title">Bulk edit selected students</h2><p id="housing-selected-count">No students selected.</p></div>
        <label class="housing-bulk-field"><span><input id="housing-bulk-rate-enabled" type="checkbox" /> Update rate choice</span>
            <select id="housing-bulk-rate" class="form-select" disabled>
                <option>Unreviewed</option><option>Standard</option><option>AIC Triple Room</option><option>Savell Triple Occupancy</option>
            </select>
        </label>
        <label class="housing-bulk-field"><span><input id="housing-bulk-notes-enabled" type="checkbox" /> Update notes</span>
            <input id="housing-bulk-notes" class="form-control" maxlength="2000" disabled />
        </label>
        <label class="housing-bulk-field"><span><input id="housing-bulk-single-enabled" type="checkbox" /> Update intentional single</span>
            <select id="housing-bulk-single" class="form-select" disabled><option value="true">Yes</option><option value="false">No</option></select>
        </label>
        <button id="housing-bulk-apply" class="btn btn-primary" type="button" disabled>Apply to selected</button>
    </section>
    <div class="housing-grid" tabindex="0" aria-label="Housing assignments table">
        <table class="table"><caption>Each empty slot represents an available bed. Choose “Assign student” to fill it.</caption>
            <thead><tr><!th scope="col"><label class="housing-select-all"><input id="housing-select-all" type="checkbox" /> Select filtered</label></!th><!th scope="col">Building / room</!th><!th scope="col">Capacity</!th><!th scope="col">Student</!th><!th scope="col">Assignment</!th><!th scope="col">Intentional single</!th><!th scope="col">Rate choice</!th><!th scope="col">Notes</!th></tr></thead>
            <tbody id="housing-rows"></tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <section id="housing-changes" hidden><h2>Change preview</h2><p>This compares the saved draft with its last refresh, including proposed housing charge lines. The Apply action checks current Elements assignments and billing before writing.</p><ul></ul></section>
    <dialog id="housing-students" aria-labelledby="housing-students-title">
        <h2 id="housing-students-title">Assign student</h2>
        <form id="housing-search-form"><label>Student ID or name <input id="housing-search" class="form-control" minlength="2" required /></label>
            <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Search</button></form>
        <div id="housing-search-results" aria-live="polite"></div>
        <button id="housing-close-search" class="btn btn-outline-secondary" type="button">Close</button>
    </dialog>
</div>
